# Rank 1262 / CVE-2024-28244: KaTeX's Parser bounds macro expansion by
# counting MacroExpander.expansionCount against settings.maxExpand on
# this.gullet, but the Unicode sub/superscript branch of parseSupSub
# (src/Parser.js) built the accumulated Unicode run into a plain string and
# handed it to a brand-new `new Parser(str, this.settings)`. That
# constructor creates its own MacroExpander, so the fresh instance's
# expansionCount starts at zero: nesting user-controlled macros inside a
# Unicode sub/superscript run resets the counter on every level and the
# expansion blows up exponentially past whatever maxExpand is configured to
# stop (GHSA-cvr6-37gx-v8wc: >= 0.15.4, < 0.16.10; CWE-606 unchecked input
# for loop condition, CWE-674 uncontrolled recursion). Fix
# 085e21b5da05414efefa932570e7201a7c70e5b2 does not touch the limit: it
# tokenizes the run and hands it to `this.subparse(subsupTokens)`, which
# pushes the tokens onto the current job's own gullet, so the existing
# expansionCount keeps accruing across the sub/superscript. The first
# release carrying the fix is v0.16.10 (`git tag --contains`); the
# fresh-Parser construct is present at v0.15.4 and absent at v0.15.3,
# matching the advisory's lower bound.
#
# The weakness is inside the library, and both revisions parse the same
# untrusted TeX string while the caller's render is correct code, so the
# report that belongs to this CVE is the dependency finding: an npm pin of
# katex below 0.16.10. The feed holds one threshold per artifact, so pins
# below the advisory's 0.15.4 lower bound report too; those releases do
# not contain the fresh-Parser construct (verified at v0.15.3) and that
# over-match is this row's stated residual.
#
# The code-level shape stays unreachable and the ENGINE-GAPS "1262" entry
# stays open: which object instance owns a resource counter is not a
# source/sink taint path, and code.UnboundedResourceOperation is populated
# only by per-language Review classifiers (Rust/Python/PHP/Ruby) plus
# narrow presence bindings, none of which generalizes to "a class
# re-instantiates itself inside its own recursive-descent method,
# discarding the counter the outer instance enforces". The two code-form
# tests below hold that gap open on both sides of the fix.

test "rank1262: a katex pin below the first maxExpand-enforcing release is a dependency finding"
  lang javascript
  file src/render.js
  code
  ```
  const katex = require('katex');

  function renderMath(req, el) {
      katex.render(req.query.tex, el, {throwOnError: false});
  }
  ```
  file package.json
  code
  ```
  {
    "name": "math-widget",
    "dependencies": {
      "katex": "0.16.9"
    }
  }
  ```
  expect VYQL-SCA-001
  expect_evidence VYQL-SCA-001 CVE-2024-28244
  expect VYQL-SCA-002

